{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall separate between the clean animal and the unclean</b> etc. It is manifest and known that clean animals are fewer than unclean animals; therefore Scripture attached the act of separation to the clean one. And likewise it is manifest and known that unclean birds are fewer than clean ones; therefore Scripture attached the act of separation to the unclean bird — for such is the practice: when the fewer and the more numerous are mixed together and one comes to separate one from the other, one separates out the fewer from the more numerous, as we learned: a person should always teach his student the short way. Complete, the section of קדושים"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:53.404114845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}